# Gimme The Loop - Workspace Rules

## 🚨 CRITICAL PROTOCOLS (STREET CODE)

All new designs, components, and graphical elements MUST be compared with the reference images in `/design` before shipping. If it doesn't vibe with the reference, it doesn't go live.

### 1. Tone & Voice

- Use street slang, local rider language. No formal/corporate talk.
- **NO EMOJIS.** Use Lucide or Phosphor icons only.
- DO NOT change copy (labels, headers, etc.) unless explicitly asked.

### 2. Visual Foundation & Branding

- **Dark Mode Only:** Main theme #1a1a1a.
- **Strict Palette:** ALWAYS use CSS variables from `:root` (--bg, --accent, --text). DO NOT use custom hex codes outside the branded palette.
- **NO ORANGE:** Do not use orange (#FF4F00) in any UI component.
- **Unified Accent:** Use only one accent color (Blue Violet #645AD0) across the whole app.
- **No Gradients:** Use solid blocks of color.
- **Spacing:** Keep it premium. Add padding if it feels tight. Content needs to breathe.
- **App Name Branding:** "GIMME THE LOOP" name must always be white (#FFFFFF). Remove all backgrounds (grey/translucent) from the brand name in the header and footer.

### 3. Layout & Components

- **Mobile-First:** Top navigation only (Logo left, Language/Burger right). Lower nav is deprecated.
- **Buttons:** Sharp 4px corners. No rounded buttons. Not full width unless necessary.
- **Hero Images:** Every page needs one. Text should sit in the lower area of the hero.
- **No New Components:** Do not create new components unless a new architectural pattern is required and specifically requested.

### 4. Technical Rules

- Ensure all interactive elements have unique IDs for testing.
- Follow existing patterns in `App.tsx` for state management and page rendering.
- Keep components focused and reusable.

### 5. DO NOT

- ...use shadows on everything.
- ...crowd the screen with buttons.
- ...use generic blue/red colors.
- ...hide the hero image with the menu overlay.
- ...ADD ANY EMOJIS (Use icons only).
- ...USE ORANGE ANYWHERE.
- ...USE MULTIPLE ACCENT COLORS; stick to Blue Violet (#645AD0).
